{
 "result": "squeeze.py is an lzma-based codec: `c` runs lzma.compress in FORMAT_RAW with LZMA2 at preset 9|EXTREME, lc=3, lp=0, pb=0, and `d` runs the matching decompress. It passes the samples and registered a baseline of 5.49301 (noise 0%). Two variants (lc=4 and lc=1 with nice_len=273 and MF_BT4) scored 5.498 and 5.481, neither beating the incumbent by the required 3%, so the body stays as is. Further lzma parameter tweaks are unlikely to clear the 3% bar, so I am stopping here to avoid spending energy on trials with little expected gain.",
